==== Flash Layout ====
Please check out the article [[docs:techref:flash.layout]]. It contains an example and a couple of explanations.

==== OEM easy installation ====

  - Download the firmware for your device:
     * Boards with 16MB flash
     * Boards with 8MB flash
  - Rename the firmware to //**openwrt.bin**//
  - Download this mtd binary (or build it your own)
     * mirror 1: {{ :media:alpha_networks:mtd-oem-asl-26555.tar.gz |}}
     * mirror 2: http://www.mediafire.com/download/8q9a75xi9w2t4o3/mtd
  - Copy //**openwrt.bin**// and //**mtd**// to a FAT32 formatted USB pendrive
  - Plug the USB pendrive to the router
  - Enter via telnet to the router and execute <code>cd /var/tmp/storage_dev/usb1_1
./mtd write openwrt.bin firmware</code>
  - Wait until it finish and reboot the router
  - Telnet to 192.168.1.1 and set a root password, or browse to http://192.168.1.1 if LuCI is installed.

Known issues: 
  - Stock firmware v2.0.0.37B_ES (Movistar España): Before flashing OpenWRT upgrade/downgrade to version [[http://cogemelamatricula.net/pub/generic_ASL-26555_ES_v2.0.0.30B_20110502.zip|v2.0.0.30B_ES]]. Access to 192.168.1.1:8000 > Maintenance > Firmware update > Wait until reboot.

==== OEM installation using the TFTP method ====
->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing.tftp]]

  * Download the firmware for your device:
     * Boards with 16MB flash
     * Boards with 8MB flash
  * Connect the [[#serial|serial]] TTL cable to interact with uBoot for loading the firmware via tftp.
  * Start a TFTP server in your PC. Copy the firmware to the server.
  * Rename the firmware to sysupgrade.bin
  * Set the IP at your pc to FIXME, and connect the ethernet cable to the router.
  * Power on the router and immediately press the **2** key at the serial console. Say **yes** for flashing the new firmware.


Known issues: The flash memory is divided into 2 regions. This may cause troubles with openwrt. Fix it from uboot command line (choose option 4):
<code>
setenv activeregion 1
saveenv
reset
</code>

==== Upgrading OpenWrt ====
->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.sysupgrade]]


FIXME

If you have already installed OpenWrt and like to reflash for e.g. upgrading to a new OpenWrt version you can upgrade using the mtd command line tool. It is important that you put the firmware image into the ramdisk (/tmp) before you start flashing.

=== LuCI Web Upgrade Process ===

  * Browse to http://192.168.1.1/cgi-bin/luci/mini/system/upgrade/ LuCI Upgrade URL
  * Upload image file for sysupgrade to LuCI
  * Wait for reboot

=== Terminal Upgrade Process ===

  * Login as root via SSH on 192.168.1.1
  * Use the following commands to upgrade.

<code>
cd /tmp/
wget http://downloads.openwrt.org/snapshots/trunk/XXX/xxx.abc
sysupgrade /tmp/xxx.abc
</code>

  *If sysupgrade does not support this router, use the following commands.

<code>
cd /tmp/
wget http://downloads.openwrt.org/snapshots/trunk/XXX/xxx.abc
mtd write /tmp/xxx.abc linux && reboot</code>


